🟠 postgres in inventory (prod-eu-1) keeps crashing because volume claim pgdata is out of space. It fails with "PANIC:  could not write to file "pg_wal/xlogtemp.31": No space left on device". Its last run lasted ten seconds; two restarts since its pod was created one hour ago. Fix in: persistentvolumeclaim/pgdata → spec.resources.requests.storage (20Gi). To check the size and capacity of the full volume claim, run kubectl describe pvc pgdata -n inventory
🟠 postgres in inventory (prod-eu-1) keeps crashing because volume claim pgdata is out of space.
| 🟠 **postgres** in **inventory** (**prod-eu-1**) keeps crashing because volume claim **pgdata** is out of space.
| It fails with
| ```
| PANIC:  could not write to file "pg_wal/xlogtemp.31": No space left on device
| ```
| Its last run lasted ten seconds; two restarts since its pod was created one hour ago.
| Fix in: persistentvolumeclaim/pgdata → spec.resources.requests.storage (20Gi).
| To check the size and capacity of the full volume claim, run
| ```
| kubectl describe pvc pgdata -n inventory
| ```
